== fm-afk-contract
ok - the read-back renders the words verbatim beside the expected return, spend cap, and reach line
ok - words preserve their final newline shape in storage and read-back
ok - one enter call writes a version 2 record, announces hold-for-return only, reads it back without asking for a go, and every read subcommand reflects it
ok - entry without --spend records the live worker count, never below the default floor, and an explicit --spend still wins
ok - live-workers counts only live work: dead, released, done, and captain-held records hold no seat
ok - a backend that cannot answer never frees a seat
ok - the retired propose, confirm, and --proposal inputs are refused by name and write nothing
ok - enter removes a proposal an older version left behind and records only the new words
ok - a same-turn entry records never-set words verbatim, adds no authority field, and restates the never-set
ok - a plain entry records no mandate in one step, and a refresh leaves the standing record untouched
ok - new words archive the old words and keep the session start
ok - a failed replacement keeps the standing posture live
ok - a failed final replacement publication rolls back its superseded archive
ok - validation and archive refuse damaged words blocks
ok - a words line that lost its record prefix fails validate, read, read-back, and archive instead of truncating the mandate
ok - archive keys the record by its entry time, empties the posture, and is idempotent
ok - malformed inputs and foreign record versions are refused rather than guessed
ok - retired clause fields, --grant, and the clause and grant subcommands are refused by name
ok - a version 1 record validates, reads its words and scalars with the clause and grant sections ignored, refreshes untouched, and archives
ok - new words over a live version 1 record archive it and write version 2 with the same session start
ok - enter and archive refuse while the record is locked, and proceed once it clears
ok - a quiet record announces, refreshes, and reads back as a present captain holding nothing, while an away record keeps hold-for-return
ok - an away entry over quiet mode records away, and a quiet entry never masks a standing away record
exit=0
== fm-capacity
ok - absent config/lane-capacity reports counts and no target
ok - the Constrained line is printed only when config/lane-capacity exists
ok - a target yields open lanes, full, and never a negative count
ok - done, dead, and captain-held records hold no lane
ok - cpu, memory, and disk pressure close every lane and are named
ok - unavailable probes print unknown and do not constrain
ok - a malformed target is reported, not guessed
ok - real host probes produce a well-formed report
# all fm-capacity tests passed
exit=0
== fm-branch-supervision
ok - middle sequence conflicts fail closed for every store read and append
ok - outcome lookup returns exact sequence rows and distinguishes missing receipts
ok - outcome stores require terminated single-line JSON records
ok - the processed marker is sequence-bound, never ahead of the read cursor, never backwards, and never adopts delivered history
ok - outcome store: present shows each routine row once and each captain row until it is acknowledged
ok - outcome store: present and unprocessed name each captain row's recorded age without writing it
ok - lease exclusivity, same-actor refresh, release, staleness, and sweep hold
ok - fm-control and fm-teardown refuse the other actor's live lease and pass through otherwise
ok - PR merge, local landing, and new-task spawn refuse the branch actor and spare main
ok - a home without a live branch lease takes no lock and clears leftover leases in any calling context
ok - an unmarked main honors a live branch lease across processes and ignores a previous session's
ok - a lease file makes an unmarked guard exclude a concurrent claim for the complete mutation
ok - a host home's unmarked main excludes the host's first claim for its whole mutation, and other homes take no lock
ok - lease liveness requires an exact valid session-lock pid
ok - a claim pinned before a re-anchor records the live lock holder; a dead pin stays stale
ok - concurrent stale-lease claims serialize so exactly one actor succeeds
ok - guard stale cleanup cannot race with or delete a newer lease claim
ok - lease guard excludes a concurrent actor for the complete mutation
ok - a claim naming the other actor fails loudly instead of silently impersonating it
ok - release commands authorize the caller and bulk release drops only that actor's leases
ok - the branch cannot force a teardown or bypass fm-control for a relaunch
ok - the away-posture record relocates the PR merge and a spawn under the spend cap to the branch, never local landing, and only while confirmed, valid, and away
ok - relocated branch spawn admits only already-queued dispatchable work, including on a manual-backend home
ok - the away spend cap is rechecked under the task-set lock so concurrent spawns cannot both publish
ok - a quiet-mode record never caps a present captain's spawn, while the away record's cap still binds
exit=0
